{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-2co-2-1","title":"2 Corinthians 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Having shown the reason why he came not to them, 6 he requires them to forgive and to comfort that excommunicated person, 10 even as himself also upon his true repentance had forgiven him; 12 declaring withal why he departed from Troas to Macedonia, 14 and the happy success which God gave to his preaching in all places.</p>\n<p>I determined. 1:15-17, Ac 11:29; 15:2,37; 1Co 2:2; 5:3; Tit 3:12 that. 4; 1:23; 7:5-8; 12:20,21; 13:10; 1Co 4:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-2","title":"2 Corinthians 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>1:14; 11:29; Ro 12:15; 1Co 12:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-3","title":"2 Corinthians 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I wrote. 1Co 4:21; 5:1-13 lest. 12:21; 13:1,2 I ought. 12:11 having. 1:15; 7:6; 8:22; Ga 5:10; Phm 1:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-4","title":"2 Corinthians 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>out. Le 19:17,18; Ps 119:136; Pr 27:5,6; Jer 13:15-17; Lu 19:41-44 Ro 9:2,3; Php 3:18 not. 7:8,9,12; 12:15 that you might. 11:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-5","title":"2 Corinthians 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>any. Pr 17:25; 1Co 5:1-5,12,13; Ga 5:10 grieved. Ga 4:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-6","title":"2 Corinthians 2:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>punishment. or, censure. which. 13:10; 1Co 5:4,5; 1Ti 5:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-7","title":"2 Corinthians 2:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>ye. Ga 6:1,2; Eph 4:32; Col 3:13; 2Th 3:6,14,15; Heb 12:12-15 swallowed. 5:4; 2Sa 20:19,20; Ps 21:9; 56:1,2; 57:3; 124:3; Pr 1:12; Isa 28:7 1Co 15:54 overmuch. 7:10; Pr 17:22; Php 2:27; 1Th 4:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-8","title":"2 Corinthians 2:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>that. Ga 5:13; 6:1,2,10; Jude 1:22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-9","title":"2 Corinthians 2:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>that. 7:12-15; 8:24; Ex 16:4; De 8:2,16; 13:3; Php 2:22 whether. 7:15; 10:6; Php 2:12; 2Th 3:14; Phm 1:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-10","title":"2 Corinthians 2:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>whom ye. 5:20; Mt 18:18; Joh 20:23; 1Co 5:4 person. or, sight.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-11","title":"2 Corinthians 2:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>11:3,14; 1Ch 21:1,2; Job 1:11; 2:3,5,9; Zec 3:1-4; Lu 22:31 Joh 13:2; Ac 1:25; 1Co 7:5; Eph 6:11,12; 2Ti 2:25; 1Pe 5:8; Re 2:24 Re 12:9-11; 13:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-12","title":"2 Corinthians 2:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>when. Ac 16:8; 20:1-6,8 and a. Ac 14:27; 1Co 16:9; Col 4:3; Re 3:7,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-13","title":"2 Corinthians 2:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>no rest. 7:5,6 Titus. 8:6,16,23; 12:18; Ga 2:1,3; 2Ti 4:10; Tit 1:4 I went. Ac 20:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-14","title":"2 Corinthians 2:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>thanks. 1:11; 8:16; 9:15; Eph 5:20; 1Th 3:9; Re 7:12 which. Ps 106:47; 148:14; Ro 8:37; 1Co 15:37 the savour. 15,16; So 1:3; Ro 15:19; Col 1:6,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-15","title":"2 Corinthians 2:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>a sweet. Ge 8:21; Ex 29:18,25; Eze 20:41; Eph 5:2; Php 4:18 in them. 4:3,4; Isa 49:5,6; 1Co 1:18; 2Th 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-16","title":"2 Corinthians 2:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the savour of death. Lu 2:34; Joh 9:39; Ac 13:45-47; 20:26,27; 1Pe 2:7,8 who. 3:5,6; 12:11; 1Co 15:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-2-17","title":"2 Corinthians 2:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>which. 4:2; 11:13-15; Jer 5:31; 23:27-32; Mt 24:24; 1Ti 1:19,20; 4:1-3 2Ti 2:6-18; 4:3,4; Tit 1:11; 2Pe 2:1-3; 1Jo 4:1; 2Jo 1:7-11; Jude 1:4 Re 2:14,15,20; 12:9; 19:20 corrupt. or, deal deceitfully with. 4:2 but as of sincerity. 1:12; 4:2; Ac 20:20,27; Heb 11:27 in. or, of.</p>"}]}